{
  "id": "urn:visionflow:page:dea1753d4e1c2addec620bedbb7729d693b3af75d55b6670ea208cc8c9ba6742",
  "title": "Bootstrap Node",
  "slug": "bootstrap-node",
  "public": true,
  "classIri": "urn:ngm:class:bootstrap-node",
  "domain": "blockchain",
  "definition": "A Bootstrap Node is a well-known, stable network entry point that newly joining peers contact to obtain their initial list of active participants in a peer-to-peer blockchain network. By providing a curated, long-lived set of peer addresses, bootstrap nodes solve the cold-start problem: without them a new client would have no means of discovering the network. They do not typically validate or store blocks themselves; their function is purely topological\u2014seeding new participants into the gossip network so that subsequent peer discovery can proceed organically.",
